  "verdict": "beta1 = 1.7538 [1.7226, 1.7850], decisively NOT 1 (the asymptotic predicts 1): the additive numerator fit is a linearization over the operating range. The interaction FORM is right -- it fits materially better at INTERPOLATION (R2 0.986 vs 0.966; pooled median rel err 4.0% vs 8.6%) and the -L*lnL term is recovered near -1 (-1.219) -- but NOT at EXTRAPOLATION: the worst held-out family (grid) goes 0.84->1.17 and the U[1,2] weight-convention holdout worsens 7.5%->11.8%.  So the leading coefficient carries a ~1.75 finite-size prefactor the leading-order expansion omits."
